{# One embedded question, fetched when its marker is reached and injected over the player (créas 5B,
   screen 4).

   Every type is rendered by the partial the passation already uses: a zone, an appariement or a
   calculée is answered inside a video exactly as it is answered inside a quiz, down to the Stimulus
   controller that drives it - Stimulus connects them on injection, so nothing here has to start
   them. That reuse is the whole feature: twelve types playable in a video without a second
   implementation of any of them.

   The form is posted by video_cue_player_controller.js as it stands, which is why the field names
   are the passation's own - App\Service\VideoCueGrader reads them under those names. #}
<div class="cm-video-cue-card">
    <div class="cm-video-cue-card__head">
        <span class="cm-badge cm-badge--blue">{{ question.type.shortLabelKey|trans }}</span>
        <span class="cm-video-cue-card__time">{{ cuePoint.formattedTimecode }}</span>
    </div>

    <form class="cm-video-cue-card__body"
          action="{{ path('app_student_work_video_cue_answer', {assignmentId: assignment.id, cueId: cuePoint.id}) }}"
          data-video-cue-player-target="form"
          data-action="submit->video-cue-player#submit"
          {{ include('quiz/_question_take_attributes.html.twig') }}>
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('student_video_cue') }}">

        {{ include('quiz/_question_take_body.html.twig') }}

        <div class="cm-video-cue-card__footer">
            {# "Passer" is here because the marker is not blocking (the default): a support that
               holds a student hostage over one question stops being a support. A blocking marker
               drops the button - the teacher asked for an answer. #}
            {% if not cuePoint.blocking %}
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm" data-action="video-cue-player#skip">{{ 'videoCueSkipAction'|trans }}</button>
            {% endif %}
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">{{ 'videoCueSubmitAction'|trans }}</button>
        </div>
    </form>
</div>
